@misc{INT7,
  title  = {Replicated FFT buffer fix integration and v0.9.1 release (INT7)},
  author = {INT7 integration worker},
  year   = {2026},
    note   = {Run pr24-20261102. INT7/RESULTS.md. Repository
              psychocoderHPC-bot/picBunch. Fixed commit 6c81ecae, merge
              9963881178, follow-up 8270bb8, release c0bf82c2251448abfaad66aa03b18ab3a9ab9322,
              tag v0.9.1 (annotated 262927baf42f26bd3fae21ac86732c3f84960bbd).
              Defect: 3-D allocUnified pads innermost row to 128 B when padded
              Mx is not a multiple of 16 doubles; pitched per-bin memset leaves
              gap bytes uncleared; contiguous FFT plan reads them as data;
              buffer reuse across velocity bins feeds bin 0 charge into later
              bins; field grows with bin count. Fix: allocate all five
              replicated-path transform buffers as flat 1-D std::size\_t counts.
              Scope: multi-bin CUDA/HIP only; single-velocity unaffected.
              picBunchFftSizeCheck validation: M=24 and M=40 free-space
              relative error 3.5e-16 to 7.0e-16 at all bin counts (was 91.6
              and 48.9 at 128 bins with 3-D buffers). Single-velocity
              regression: 20-cell mesh-only and accuracy anchor bitwise
              unchanged (SHA-256 verified). 19/19 CTest on hal (HIP gfx1100)
              and fwk394 (CUDA 12.5, sm\_70).},
 }
